{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_02eb709316f49443016a9bc221cbe087d19180492419a190a4","text":"1. Apple is crisp and sweet. It grows on trees in many colors.\n\n2. Banana is soft and creamy. It comes in a peel.\n\n3. Orange is juicy and bright. Its citrus flavor is tangy.\n\n4. Strawberry is red and fragrant. Its seeds sit on the outside.\n\n5. Blueberry is small and deep blue. It has a pleasantly sweet flavor.\n\n6. Raspberry is delicate and richly flavored. It is made of many tiny drupelets.\n\n7. Blackberry is dark and glossy. It tastes sweet with a little tartness.\n\n8. Grapefruit is large and citrusy. Its flesh can range from pink to red.\n\n9. Lemon is sharply sour. Its zest adds fragrance to food.\n\n10. Lime is small and green. It gives drinks a fresh tart kick.\n\n11. Grape grows in clustered bunches. It can be eaten fresh or dried into raisins.\n\n12. Watermelon has cool, watery flesh. It is especially popular in summer.\n\n13. Cantaloupe is a muskmelon with orange flesh. It has a sweet floral aroma.\n\n14. Honeydew melon has pale green flesh. It is mellow and refreshing.\n\n15. Pineapple has a spiky skin. Its golden flesh is sweet and acidic.\n\n16. Mango is silky and tropical. Its large pit sits at the center.\n\n17. Papaya has soft orange flesh. Its hollow center contains black seeds.\n\n18. Kiwi has fuzzy brown skin. Inside, it is vivid green with tiny seeds.\n\n19. Peach is velvety and juicy. It has a hard stone in the middle.\n\n20. Nectarine resembles a peach. Its skin is smooth rather than fuzzy.\n\n21. Plum has smooth skin and a stone. It can be sweet or pleasantly tart.\n\n22. Apricot is small and golden. Its flavor is both sweet and tangy.\n\n23. Cherry is round and glossy. Most varieties contain a central pit.\n\n24. Pear has a gentle sweetness. Its texture becomes buttery when ripe.\n\n25. Pomegranate holds jewel-like arils. Each aril contains a seed and juice.\n\n26. Fig has a soft, honeyed interior. It is actually a cluster of tiny flowers.\n\n27. Date is chewy and very sweet. It grows on date palms.\n\n28. Coconut has a tough fibrous husk. Its interior provides white flesh and water.\n\n29. Avocado is creamy and mild. Botanically, it is a large berry.\n\n30. Passion fruit has wrinkled purple or yellow skin. Its pulpy center is intensely aromatic.\n\n31. Guava has a tropical perfume. Its flesh may be white, pink, or red.\n\n32. Lychee has rough red skin. Its translucent flesh is sweet and floral.\n\n33. Rambutan looks like a hairy lychee. Its juicy white flesh surrounds a seed.\n\n34. Dragon fruit has vivid pink skin. Its speckled flesh is mild and refreshing.\n\n35. Star fruit is shaped like a star when sliced. It has crisp, juicy flesh.\n\n36. Persimmon is orange and glossy. Ripe varieties can taste like honey.\n\n37. Cranberry is bright red and tart. It is often sweetened for sauces and drinks.\n\n38. Gooseberry is small and round. Its flavor ranges from sour to sweet.\n\n39. Currant grows in tiny clusters. It is often used in jams and baked goods.\n\n40. Mulberry is elongated and deeply colored. It stains easily when fully ripe.\n\n41. Elderberry is small and dark purple. It is commonly cooked into syrups or preserves.\n\n42. Boysenberry is a blackberry hybrid. It has a bold, sweet-tart taste.\n\n43. Loganberry is another bramble hybrid. It resembles a long raspberry.\n\n44. Kumquat is a tiny citrus fruit. Its peel is sweet while its interior is tart.\n\n45. Tangerine is easy to peel. It is sweeter than many oranges.\n\n46. Clementine is a small seedless citrus. It is convenient for snacking.\n\n47. Pomelo is the largest citrus fruit. Its flesh is milder than grapefruit.\n\n48. Yuzu is a fragrant Japanese citrus. Its juice and peel flavor many dishes.\n\n49. Satsuma is a loose-skinned mandarin. It is notably juicy and sweet.\n\n50. Jackfruit is enormous and tropical. Its ripe pods can taste like a mix of fruits.\n\n51. Durian has a spiky shell. Its aroma is famously strong.\n\n52. Breadfruit has starchy flesh. It is often cooked like a vegetable.\n\n53. Plantain is firmer than a dessert banana. It is usually cooked before eating.\n\n54. Quince is hard when raw. Cooking turns it fragrant and rosy.\n\n55. Loquat is small and orange. It has a sweet-tart, apricot-like flavor.\n\n56. Medlar is an unusual brown fruit. It becomes edible after softening.\n\n57. Salak is called snake fruit. Its scaly skin hides crisp pale flesh.\n\n58. Feijoa has green oval skin. Its flavor suggests pineapple and guava.\n\n59. Soursop has spiny green skin. Its white flesh is creamy and tangy.\n\n60. Açaí is a dark purple berry. It is commonly served frozen in bowls.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null},"threadId":"01a0706e-47e0-7243-ade7-d2eb280bd202","turnId":"01a0706e-49ed-76e2-b2ec-d538c9edd117","completedAtMs":1788592697078},"emittedAtMs":1788592697080}
